# Openbox Workstation — XSETTINGS configuration
#
# Purpose:
#   Publish session-wide X11 font-rendering and DPI settings through the
#   XSETTINGS protocol. This is especially important in a bare Openbox
#   session, where no desktop settings daemon is otherwise available.
#
# Why it is needed:
#   Some applications, including Java/Swing applications such as MATLAB,
#   do not obtain all font-rendering information directly from GTK config
#   files. Their text rendering improves when an XSETTINGS manager is active.
#
# Scope:
#   Keep this file limited to DPI, antialiasing, hinting and subpixel order.
#   GTK theme, icon theme, cursor theme and GTK font family are configured
#   separately in gtkrc-2.0 and gtk-3.0/settings.ini.
#
# Notes:
#   - Xft/DPI is expressed as DPI multiplied by 1024.
#   - 98304 means 96 DPI.
#   - Only one XSETTINGS manager should run in the session.
#   - Do not run xsettingsd (a standalone application) and xfsettingsd 
#     (a XFCE4-settings daemon) simultaneously.

Xft/DPI 98304
Xft/Antialias 1
Xft/Hinting 1
Xft/HintStyle "hintmedium"
Xft/RGBA "rgb"


# THEREFORE, DO NOT ALLOW xsettingsd TO CONTROL GTK ELEMENTS LIKE BELOW.
#
#  - Net/ThemeName "Yaru"
#  - Net/IconThemeName "Papirus"
#  - Gtk/FontName "Inter 11"

# This arrangement keeps the configuration predictable:
#   xsettingsd
#   └── DPI and font rendering for the X11 session
#
#   gtkrc-2.0
#   └── GTK 2 appearance
#   
#   gtk-3.0/settings.ini
#   └── GTK 3 appearance
